Visual Prompt Studio 1.1- The Sci-Fi Film Poster Challenge

Create a sci-fi film poster showing a person in a small boat in the middle of the ocean at night, escaping from something unknown and traveling toward another galaxy visible in the distance. Use wavy lines in the ocean and curved lines in the galaxy to guide the viewer’s eyes toward the bright galaxy and create a sense of movement. This layout creates a mysterious, lonely, and emotional atmosphere. Make the galaxy the main focal point by using bright purple, blue, and white colors against the dark sky and ocean. Use negative space to emphasize the enormous universe and make the boat look small and isolated. Give the ocean a rough texture and the boat a solid, weathered appearance to create depth and volume.
In the final poster, the galaxy stands out the most because of its brightness, size, and strong contrast. The colors, scale, and composition help direct attention toward it. However, the AI misunderstood part of my original idea because it did not show what the person was escaping from, and the boat looked stronger than I imagined. For my second attempt, change only the color palette from cool blues and purples to warm oranges and reds. This adjustment makes the poster feel more dangerous, intense, and dramatic instead of calm and mysterious. It shows how color can completely change the mood of an image.

Vocabulary Breakdown: In the poster, lines are used in the ocean waves and the spiral galaxy to guide the viewer’s eyes toward the focal point; shape is shown through the circular galaxy and the small boat that help organize the composition; texture appears in the rough ocean surface and the weathered boat, making them look more realistic; volume is created through lighting and perspective, giving the boat, waves, and galaxy a three-dimensional appearance; and contrast is achieved by placing the bright galaxy against the dark night sky and ocean, making it stand out as the most important element in the image.

